   "unmapped": [
    "Multinomial logit (MNL) choice feedback: the learner observes which item (or no purchase) the customer chooses from the offered assortment, with probability v_j/(1+sum_{j' in S} v_{j'})",
    "Reward is the expected revenue R_v(S) = sum r_i v_i / (1 + sum v_i), nonlinear in the assortment",
    "The learner knows the revenue parameters r_i (in (0,1]); preference parameters v_i unknown"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "In this model, $N$ items are present, each associated with a known revenue parameter $r_i>0$ and an unknown preference parameter $v_i>0$. For a total of $T$ epochs, at each epoch $t$ a retailer ... selects an \\emph{assortment} $S_t\\subseteq[N]$ of size at most $K$ ... The retailer then observes a purchasing outcome $i_t\\in S_t\\cup\\{0\\}$ sampled from ... $\\Pr[i_t=j] = \\frac{v_j}{1+\\sum_{j'\\in S_t}v_{j'}}$"
  }
